WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
Here is a horseshoe
magnet: north pole on top,

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:06.610
south pole below, and a gap between them.

3
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:10.340
Run a straight wire across the
gap, and switch on a current.

4
00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:14.510
A wire carrying a current in a
magnetic field feels a force.

5
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.580
Reverse the current:
the force reverses too.

6
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.150
So which way is the wire pushed?

7
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.400
In this mission, you'll learn a hand rule
that gives the direction of the force.

8
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:30.220
Then you'll calculate its size:
2.5 amps in a field of 0.15 tesla,

9
00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:32.360
on a short length of wire.

10
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:35.530
Your mission: predict which
way the wire is pushed,

11
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.750
and explain why.
